0.08 0.17 0.24 rg BT /F1 9.75 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.00 254.30 Tm (Why a ladder instead of a danger score? A numeric score does not tell the officer what may safely happen next. The) Tj ET
0.08 0.17 0.24 rg BT /F1 9.75 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.00 239.90 Tm (ladder converts evidence into progressively more consequential actions, with an explicit boundary between automated) Tj ET
0.08 0.17 0.24 rg BT /F1 9.75 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.00 225.50 Tm (steps and human authority. It also makes the "gentlest response" testable: the receipt can explain why one rung lower) Tj ET
0.08 0.17 0.24 rg BT /F1 9.75 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.00 211.10 Tm (would be insufficient and one rung higher would be excessive.) Tj ET
0.08 0.17 0.24 rg BT /F1 9.75 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.00 187.70 Tm (Why model consequence as well as classification? A contact's label does not determine its effect on a harbor. The) Tj ET
0.08 0.17 0.24 rg BT /F1 9.75 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.00 173.30 Tm (same unknown object far from operations is different from an unknown object beside a fuel transfer or diver area.) Tj ET
0.08 0.17 0.24 rg BT /F1 9.75 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.00 158.90 Tm (Distance, projected motion, and operations in progress make the decision situational. Classification confidence is) Tj ET
0.08 0.17 0.24 rg BT /F1 9.75 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.00 144.50 Tm (treated as evidence, not as a substitute for consequence or intent.) Tj ET
0.08 0.17 0.24 rg BT /F1 9.75 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.00 121.10 Tm (Why a bounded second look? More sensor evidence is cheap compared with stopping work or paging a person, but an) Tj ET
0.08 0.17 0.24 rg BT /F1 9.75 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.00 106.70 Tm (unbounded loop would quietly defer a decision forever. Two looks with a time limit make "look again" a real rung) Tj ET
0.08 0.17 0.24 rg BT /F1 9.75 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.00 92.30 Tm (rather than a hiding place for uncertainty.) Tj ET
0.08 0.17 0.24 rg BT /F1 9.75 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.00 68.90 Tm (Why put AI behind rules? A network model adds latency, cost, and output uncertainty. The deterministic rules cover) Tj ET
